# Limitations and Future Scope

## Current Limitations

### 1. No Actual Hill Deployment

The prototype was not deployed at an actual hill location during the initial project demonstration.

### 2. No Soil-Based Vibration Validation

The vibration sensor was not installed inside actual soil/ground conditions for field validation.

### 3. Controlled Test Inputs

The demonstrated alert responses were verified using controlled/programmed test conditions rather than long-term natural environmental data.

### 4. Component Protection

A field-deployable version requires a suitable protective and water-resistant enclosure before placing sensors/electronics in outdoor or soil environments.

---

## Future Scope

### Soil-Based Vibration Monitoring

A suitable ground vibration sensing arrangement can be developed for actual soil/ground testing.

### Rugged Enclosure

The electronics can be protected using an outdoor-rated enclosure with appropriate water, dust and mechanical protection.

### LoRaWAN

LoRaWAN can be explored for long-range communication in remote locations.

### GPS

GPS can be added to provide the location of an emergency event.

### GSM/SMS

GSM can provide an alternative notification mechanism.

### Solar Power

Solar and battery-based power can support longer outdoor operation.

### Predictive Analytics

Long-term sensor data can be used for future machine-learning-based risk analysis.
